================================================================================
Optional extras
================================================================================

The `[semantic]` extra (sentence-transformers, numpy) is not installed by
default. On Linux it additionally pulls torch and its transitive NVIDIA CUDA
runtime packages (e.g. nvidia-cublas, nvidia-cudnn, nvidia-cufft, triton),
which are governed by NVIDIA's CUDA EULA / Apache-2.0 and torch's BSD-style
license. These are resolved and accepted by the end user; cairn does not
bundle or redistribute them.

The embedding model `BAAI/bge-m3` (referenced by name, downloaded on demand
to ~/.cairn/lib/ when a user runs `cg embed --install-deps`) is released
under the MIT License on Hugging Face. cairn does not redistribute the
model weights.

================================================================================
Vendored content (benchmark corpus)
================================================================================

The datasource benchmarks vendor a source snapshot of one third-party project
solely as benchmark content. Unlike the packages above, this snapshot is
carried in-tree; it is not a runtime dependency and no part of it is imported
by cairn's code.

yarl (https://github.com/aio-libs/yarl), Copyright 2016-2021, Andrew Svetlov
and aio-libs team. Vendored at pinned commit
dddcb82e4aa9665e15b43d90ad370d7e54ac1fbb (GitHub source export taken
2026-08-15) under benchmarks/datasource/t2/yarl/, and licensed under
Apache-2.0. The full license text is retained in-tree, unmodified, at
benchmarks/datasource/t2/yarl/LICENSE; the complete export record (origin,
pin, license, kept and excluded files, and size) is kept alongside the
snapshot in benchmarks/datasource/t2/provenance.json.
